# RodNIX kernel configuration -- machine-independent options.
#
# This file answers "what is this kernel", separately from "how is it
# built" (makedefs/) and "what files exist" (<component>/conf/files).
# It is the RodNIX counterpart of XNU's config/MASTER and FreeBSD's
# sys/<arch>/conf/GENERIC.
#
# Each line here does two things: it lets a manifest select sources with
# "optional <NAME>", and it reaches the compiler as -D<NAME>. Turning an
# option off means commenting the line out, so the file always reads as a
# list of what is in, never a list of what was taken out.
#
# Machine-dependent options belong in config/MASTER.<arch>.

options		IDL_DEMO	# in-kernel IDL round-trip demonstration
